course: dictionary
lesson: 1056
title: Botanical: words about plants
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Botanical means to do with plants, or with botany, the science of plants. A botanical garden is a garden where plants from around the world are grown, labelled and studied. «...ended his life working in a botanical garden.» The garden is full of plants, so botanical must be about plants.
explain: Botanical can also mean made from plants. Botanical oils and botanical medicines come from plants, not from metal or chemicals.
explain: Scientists use the word botanical when they talk about plant names. Every plant has a botanical name in Latin, so that people in different countries can all know which plant they mean. Bellis perennis is the botanical name for the daisy.
fact: Botany is the science of plants.
fact: A botanical garden, also called a botanic garden, grows plants from around the world and labels them.
fact: Kew Gardens in London is a famous botanical garden.
fact: A botanical drawing is a careful, detailed picture of a plant, often used by scientists.
fact: A botanical name is the scientific name of a plant, usually in Latin, such as Bellis perennis for the daisy.
exercise: «...ended his life working in a botanical garden.» Where did Puyi work at the end of his life? | A school | A railway station | *A botanical garden | A royal palace
exercise: In «Botanical drawings are careful, detailed pictures of plants», what does botanical mean? | To do with machines | To do with the sea | *To do with plants | Very fast
exercise: Every plant has a botanical name in Latin, such as Bellis perennis for the daisy. What is the botanical name of the daisy? | Kew Gardens | Daisy | *Bellis perennis | Latin
test: In science, a botanical garden is a place where plants from around the world are grown, labelled and studied. What happens there? | Only one type of tree grows | Only cats live there | Cars are repaired | *Plants from around the world are grown, labelled and studied
test: Botanical oils and medicines are made from what? | Plastic | Metal | Sand | *Plants
exam: In «a botanical garden», which meaning of botanical fits best? | Very old | Made of stone | Full of water | *To do with plants
